// lexdb over TNS: the eighth bug slice (design/lexdb-robust.md, "The eighth bug slice"; KNOWN-ISSUES.md), checked against Oracle Database Free
// 23.26 (gen_oracle.py --check tns_bugs8): the overloaded members of a package, picked by the call's arguments as Oracle does (their number, names
// and type families: number, varchar2, date), from SQL (a SELECT list, a WHERE, a view, INSERT ... SELECT) and from PL/SQL, whichever the order of
// the declarations; arguments by name (name => value) of a package's and of a standalone function in SQL; ORA-06553 (PLS-306, PLS-307) for a call in
// SQL that none or more than one declaration fits, ORA-06550 in a block. Each statement runs with set lexdb_batch = off (the row engine) and on:
// "same" and the answer, or DIFFERENT and both.
// expect: setup: 22 statements
// expect: same: A = 16
// expect: same: A = 3
// expect: same: A = 7
